---
/**
 * The connecting line.
 *
 * A 1px --color-signal hairline on the page's centre axis, occupying the gap
 * between every pair of sections from the hero down to the footer. Because
 * every gap carries it at the same x, the eye reads one continuous span top
 * to bottom — the crossing, stated structurally rather than illustrated.
 *
 * It is never an arrow, never labelled, never a gradient. It stays
 * subordinate to the card render, which is the page's only loud object.
 * Hidden below 768px, where the single-column rhythm carries the page on its
 * own and a centre line would only crowd it.
 *
 * Purely decorative, so it is hidden from assistive technology.
 */
---

<div class="bridge-span" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  .bridge-span {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .bridge-span {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      height: 64px;
    }

    .bridge-span::before {
      content: '';
      width: 1px;
      height: 100%;
      background-color: var(--color-signal);
      /* Quiet enough that most visitors register it as rhythm, not as a
         drawn element. */
      opacity: 0.5;
    }
  }
</style>
